; A balance assignment leaves out earlier postings dated after it, and a
; posting's date can come from a note in two ways besides its own line:
; a posting generated by an automated transaction takes the date of the
; posting it was generated from, and a posting whose amount is elided
; keeps the date its note gives it.  Both are dated 2024/03/01 here, so
; the assignments of 2024/02/01 do not count them.

= /^Expenses:Food$/
    (Budget:Food)                         -1

2024/01/01 Opening
    (Budget:Food)                       $100
    Assets:Checking                     $100
    Equity:Opening

2024/01/05 Lunch
    Expenses:Food                        $10  ; [2024/03/01]
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/06 Dinner
    Expenses:Dining                      $20
    Assets:Checking  ; [2024/03/01]

2024/02/01 Reset budget
    (Budget:Food)                             = $0

2024/02/01 Sweep checking
    Assets:Checking                           = $0
    Assets:Savings

test bal
                 $70  Assets
                $-10    Cash
                $-20    Checking
                $100    Savings
                $-10  Budget:Food
               $-100  Equity:Opening
                 $30  Expenses
                 $20    Dining
                 $10    Food
--------------------
                $-10
end test

test reg --sort date Budget Checking
24-Jan-01 Opening               (Budget:Food)                  $100         $100
                                Assets:Checking                $100         $200
24-Feb-01 Reset budget          (Budget:Food)                 $-100         $100
24-Feb-01 Sweep checking        Assets:Checking               $-100            0
24-Mar-01 Lunch                 (Budget:Food)                  $-10         $-10
24-Mar-01 Dinner                Assets:Checking                $-20         $-30
end test
